  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before 3 February 2023.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (K/595/01/A, K/595/02/A, K/595/03/A, K/595/04/A, LP/01 - received 5th July 2022 and Energy and Sustainability Assessment by Watt Energy & Consulting Engineers - received 14th January 2020) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials used in the development, the cycle parking provision, boundary treatment and hard and soft landscaping shall be implemented before the development is first occupied in accordance with the details approved under planning decision reference 00203/6/P3(3-10) dated 18 March 2022.",
    "Condition : 4 - The development shall meet the following sustainable materials standards and shall not be occupied until evidence (e.g. photographs and copies of delivery notes, invoices or installation contracts) has been submitted to the Local Planning Authority to show that the development meets the following:\r\n\"\tAt least three of the key elements of the building envelope (external walls, windows roof, upper floor slabs, internal walls, floor finishes/coverings) are to achieve a rating of A+ to D in the Building Research Establishment (BRE) The Green Guide of specification.\r\n\"\tAt least 50% of timber and timber products are to be sourced from accredited Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) or Programme for the Endorsement of Forestry Certification (PEFC) scheme.\r\n\"\tNo construction or insulation materials are to be used which will release toxins into the internal and external environment, including those that deplete stratospheric ozone.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to first occupation of the building(s) evidence (e.g. photographs, installation contracts and As-Built certificates under the Standard Assessment Procedure shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing to show that the development has been constructed in accordance with the Energy Strategy approved under planning decision reference 00203/6/P3 dated 3 February 2020.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to first occupation of the building(s) evidence (schedule of fittings and manufacturers' literature) shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing to show that the development has achieved an internal water use of 105 litres/person/day or less.",
    "Condition : 7 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 2015 (as amended) (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site (delineated by the red line submitted as part of the application) shall be carried out, nor shall any vehicle access be formed to the adjacent highway.",
    "Condition : 8 - No additional windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the walls of the development hereby approved and no additional doors inserted in the building and the first floor landing window facing .2 Newgate Close shall be in obscure glazing and unopenable and shall be so retained permanently."
  ],
